  "nl_text": "The rschema_0276 database is designed to manage information related to maintenance services provided to customers. It consists of five tables: maintenance_technician, maintenance_team, customer, maintenance_task, and maintenance_feedback. The maintenance_technician table stores details about the technicians, including their unique identifier, name, gender, phone number, position, employment date, and the team they belong to, with the team_id referencing the customer table. The maintenance_team table contains information about the teams, such as the team's unique identifier, name, leader's identifier, responsibilities, and total number of members, with the team_leader_id referencing the maintenance_technician table. The customer table holds details about the customers, including their unique identifier, name, phone number, and address. The maintenance_task table stores records of maintenance tasks, including the task's unique identifier, customer identifier, maintenance cost, duration, result, time, and the technician who performed the task, with the customer_id referencing the customer table and the maintenance_technician referencing the maintenance_technician table. The maintenance_feedback table contains feedback from customers regarding the maintenance tasks, including the task's unique identifier, feedback content, resolution result, and customer satisfaction, with the maintenance_task_number referencing the maintenance_task table. The database uses InnoDB as its storage engine and UTF-8mb3 as its character set.",
  "gold_question": "The maintenance task management system shall be utilized for managing maintenance technicians, maintenance teams, customer information, and records related to maintenance tasks. The system shall support the assignment and management of maintenance tasks, record customer information during the maintenance process, including maintenance costs, duration, results, and collect customer feedback and satisfaction levels. The system may store the following information:  \nMaintenance Technician Table: Stores personal information of maintenance technicians, including technician name, gender, phone number, position, employment date, and team ID.  \n\nManagement Maintenance Team: Stores relevant information of maintenance teams, including team name, team leader ID, team responsibilities, and total number of members.  \n\nManagement Customer: Stores personal information of customers, including customer name, phone number, and address.  \n\nManagement Maintenance Task: Records detailed information for each maintenance task, including maintenance time, maintenance duration, costs, results, customer feedback, and model and name of the maintenance product. Each maintenance task also records customer satisfaction levels and feedback resolution results.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_llama31/0276.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0276\nCREATE TABLE `maintenance_technician` (\n  `technician_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `gender` char(1) NOT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(15) NOT NULL,\n  `position` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `employment_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `team_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`technician_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `maintenance_technician_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`team_id`) REFERENCES `maintenance_team` (`team_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `maintenance_team` (\n  `team_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `team_leader_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `responsibilities` text NOT NULL,\n  `total_members` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`team_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `maintenance_team_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`team_leader_id`) REFERENCES `maintenance_technician` (`technician_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `customer` (\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(15) NOT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`customer_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `maintenance_task` (\n  `task_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `maintenance_cost` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `duration` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `result` text NOT NULL,\n  `time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `technician_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`task_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `maintenance_task_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `customer` (`customer_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `maintenance_task_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`technician_id`) REFERENCES `maintenance_technician` (`technician_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `maintenance_feedback` (\n  `feedback_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `task_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `feedback_content` text NOT NULL,\n  `resolution_result` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `customer_satisfaction` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`feedback_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `maintenance_feedback_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`task_id`) REFERENCES `maintenance_task` (`task_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
